3. Built-in wordlists (wordbanks/*.json) — headwords, phonetics, glosses
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Used in: wordbanks/*.json (the `word`, `phonetic` and `explains` fields;
         the same fields appear in the mini-program copies under
         mobile/wordbank-json/*.json, which are not part of this package;
         the derived `freq` ranking fields are covered by section 2 above)

The headword lists are compiled from the public examination syllabi the
lists are named after (中考/高考/CET-4/CET-6/考研/TOEFL/IELTS/BEC/GRE/GMAT
等大纲词汇表). Syllabus word lists are factual compilations. The `phonetic`
fields use standard IPA notation. The `explains` fields are brief,
dictionary-style Chinese glosses (part of speech plus common meanings) of
the kind shared across exam vocabulary handbooks; they are short factual
study notes rather than creative text, and no single upstream dictionary is
reproduced in full.

If you are a rights holder and believe any entry infringes your rights,
please open an issue in this repository; affected entries will be removed
or replaced with self-written glosses.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Built-in Chinese poetry & prose corpus
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Used in: datafile/poetry/*.json (xianqin/han/weijin/sui/tang/song/yuan/
         ming/qing/xiandai) and datafile/idioms/*.json

The classical texts (先秦 through 清) are public-domain works. The 近现代
(xiandai) section contains only works that have entered the public domain
in China (author deceased for more than 50 years: 徐志摩、戴望舒、闻一多);
works still under copyright are not included. Pinyin annotations are
generated by this project's own scripts (scripts/add-poetry-pinyin.cjs).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. Built-in foreign-language classics
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Used in: datafile/english/*.json (speeches, poems, essays, bilingual,
         japanese, french, russian)

Speeches, poems, essays and the japanese/french/russian selections are
public-domain originals (e.g. Lincoln, Shakespeare, Shelley, Bacon,
清少納言、松尾芭蕉、プルースト、モーテーニュ、ボードレール、プーシキン).
The bilingual category ships English originals only; no translated text is
bundled without a named translator. Works that are still under copyright in
China (or whose Chinese translation has no named translator) are excluded
from every build, not only the store build; the removed entries are kept in
archive/restricted-content/english/ for traceability.

movie-scripts.json (short quotations from films) is not included in any
build; the file has been moved to archive/restricted-content/ because the
underlying screenplays are still under copyright. It will only return if
written permission is obtained.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. Pre-generated speech audio
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Used in: speech-audio/spoken-reactions-1/*.mp3 and
         speech-audio/spoken-reductions-1/*.mp3 (500 files each)

These are synthetic speech files generated offline by this project's
maintainers with edge-tts (https://github.com/rany2/edge-tts, an unofficial
client for the Microsoft Edge online TTS service), using the neural voice
en-US-AvaNeural. File names are MD5("{voice}|{rate}|{normalized text}") and
match the lookup scheme in src/utils/speech-audio.ts. The spoken texts are
the entries of the bundled spoken-reactions-1 / spoken-reductions-1
wordbanks. The audio is distributed as pre-generated study material so the
feature works without a network TTS request; it is not a recording of any
copyrighted audiobook or broadcast.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
7. Project-authored content and AI assistance
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Used in: wordbanks/*.json, datafile/poetry/*.json (pinyin and tags),
         datafile/idioms/*.json, knowledgebanks/*.json,
         datafile/timeline/*.json and the shortcut/phonetic datasets

Word lists, Chinese explanations, example sentences, knowledge-pack entries
(science, history, geography and common-sense items), idiom entries and
timeline events are compiled by this project's maintainers or drafted with
the help of large language models and then edited. They are provided for
personal memory practice. They are not official examination syllabi,
textbooks or teaching material, and this project is not affiliated with any
examination authority or publisher.

Film and TV word banks, film dialogue and quotations from films are not
included in any build (moved to archive/restricted-content/). Modern Chinese
poems in datafile/poetry are limited to works that have entered the public
domain in China.

If you are a rights holder and believe an entry infringes your rights,
please open an issue in this repository and the entry will be removed.
